# The lanes of the host's pair rows against the scalar row on a dense
# system, at the bound of the order of a sum (D[host-pair-vector];
# Inputs/host_pair_lanes_bound.py says how the bound is made). The dipeptide
# in water with PME: ten types, the exclusions of its topology, rows of 83 to
# 275 candidates, most of them not a multiple of the width, so that the
# padding of a tail repeats a candidate that contributes. lanes(8) and
# lanes(4) at step 0 in double and mixed precision: every force component
# and the potential within the bound. A tail whose padding is not masked
# gives ratios of 1e10; a skipped or a doubled candidate, a gather of the
# wrong lane, or a wrong reduction would do as much.
#
# REQUIRES: python-api, parmed
#
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/host_pair_lanes_bound.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide Double 8 4 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/host_pair_lanes_bound.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide Mixed 8 4 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED

# DOUBLE: rows: 83 to 275 candidates within the cutoff
# DOUBLE: Double lanes(8): {{.*}}: within the bound
# DOUBLE: Double lanes(4): {{.*}}: within the bound
# DOUBLE: all within the bound
# MIXED: Mixed lanes(8): {{.*}}: within the bound
# MIXED: Mixed lanes(4): {{.*}}: within the bound
# MIXED: all within the bound
